sections.body:
A **feature** is an input variable the model uses. **Feature engineering** turns raw data into useful inputs:
- encoding categorical values (one-hot encoding for unordered categories);
- scaling numeric values so features on large scales do not dominate distance-based or gradient-based methods;
- deriving new signals (day of week from a timestamp, ratios, text statistics).

Deep learning reduces the need for hand-made features on unstructured data (images, text) because the network **learns representations**, but tabular problems still benefit from careful features. In NLP, classic pipelines use libraries such as spaCy for tokenisation, part-of-speech tags and named entities, and NumPy arrays to hold the resulting numeric features.
